=== 0: shift past the end fails with status 1
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|shift: 1

=== 1: A non-numeric shift count is misuse, in bash's words
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|shift x: 2
|shift: x: numeric argument required

=== 2: shift with a negative count reports it and fails with status 1
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|shift -1: 1 2
|reported
|shift -0: 0 2

=== 3: shift takes --
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|0 c

=== 4: shift with too many arguments abandons the rest of the line
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|next line: 2 2
--- stderr
|bash: line 2: shift: too many arguments
